+issueNumber: MDL-70225
+notes:
+  search_simpledb:
+    - message: >-
+        The simple search engine now matches the start of words instead of
+        requiring exact word matches. Every term in the query is required
+        (AND) and each of them matches any word beginning with it, e.g.
+        searching for 'Cat 10' finds 'Cats 101'. Substrings in the middle of
+        a word (e.g. 'ogs') are not matched.
+      type: improved
